{
  "info": {
    "name": "Shiparc.AI - Combined Engagement Score API",
    "description": "Functional, negative, auth, and security tests for GET /api/admin/dashboard/engagement/combined-engagement-score (Company Admin Home dashboard).\n\nIMPORTANT - AUTH SETUP: the login endpoint blocks scripted clients (Postman, Newman, raw HTTP requests) even with correct credentials, so this collection authenticates via a manually-pasted session cookie instead of scripting the login - see Login_Flow_Notes.md for why.\n\nWORKAROUND (do this first):\n1. Log into https://project.shiparc.ai/ as Company Admin in a real browser.\n2. Open DevTools > Network, find any authenticated request (e.g. combined-engagement-score), open its Headers tab, and copy the value of the session cookie from the Request Headers 'cookie' line - the one starting with '__Secure-next-auth.session-token' (NextAuth may split a large JWT across '__Secure-next-auth.session-token', '.0', '.1' etc. - if so, verify the exact cookie name(s) in your browser's Cookies tab and concatenate the values in order).\n3. Paste that value into this collection's 'admin_session_cookie' variable (Variables tab, 'CURRENT VALUE' column).\n4. Repeat with a Crew-role login to fill in 'crew_session_cookie' (needed only for A-02).\n5. In Postman Settings > General, turn on 'Disable cookies' - otherwise Postman's own cookie jar can auto-attach a stray session cookie to A-01, which is deliberately testing the no-cookie case.\n6. Run '0. SETUP' first to confirm the pasted cookie actually authenticates, then run folders 1-4 in any order.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "https://project.shiparc.ai" },
    { "key": "company_id", "value": "cmgrlybyk00uqrzs7j3eq3hrf" },
    { "key": "vessel_id", "value": "cmgt4qqg4000rs0qjcd1lx2vr" },
    { "key": "session_cookie_name", "value": "__Secure-next-auth.session-token" },
    { "key": "admin_session_cookie", "value": "PASTE_ADMIN_SESSION_COOKIE_VALUE_HERE", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "crew_session_cookie", "value": "PASTE_CREW_SESSION_COOKIE_VALUE_HERE", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. SETUP (read me first)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Verify pasted admin session cookie works",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Cookie", "value": "{{session_cookie_name}}={{admin_session_cookie}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/session",
            "description": "Scripted login is blocked by this app's anti-automation protection (see collection description and Login_Flow_Notes.md). This request does NOT log in - it just confirms that the session cookie you manually pasted into 'admin_session_cookie' is valid, by calling NextAuth's own /api/auth/session endpoint and checking it returns the admin user. If this fails, re-copy the cookie value from a fresh browser login (session cookies expire/rotate)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('session has a user (cookie is valid)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
